                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "Here are the recommendations for your trip to Paris:\n\n### Restaurant Recommendations\n1. **Le Baratin**\n   - **Rating:** 4.8\n   - **Address:** 3 Rue Jouye-Rouve, 75020 Paris, France\n   - **Reviews:** Small, cozy bistro with delicious, homestyle cooking. Daily changing menu based on fresh market ingredients. Natural wine selection. Cash only.\n\n2. **Bistrot Paul Bert**\n   - **Rating:** 4.5\n   - **Address:** 18 Rue Paul Bert, 75011 Paris, France\n   - **Reviews:** One of the best classic French bistros in Paris. Excellent steak tartare and pommes frites. Charming old-school Parisian atmosphere. Reservations recommended.\n\n3. **Chez L'Ami Jean**\n   - **Rating:** 4.4\n   - **Address:** 27 Rue Malar, 75007 Paris, France\n   - **Reviews:** Michelin-starred Basque-influenced cuisine. Famous rice pudding dessert. Lively, bustling atmosphere. Reservations essential.\n\n### Hotel Recommendations\n1. **Le Marais Boutique**\n   - **Price Range:** 120.0 - 180.0 euros\n   - **Address:** 12 Rue des Archives, 75004 Paris, France\n\n2. **Good Night**\n   - **Price Range:** 240.0 - 400.0 euros\n   - **Address:** 15 Rue Cler, 75007 Paris, France\n\n3. **Montmartre Suites**\n   - **Price Range:** 110.0 - 200.0 euros\n   - **Address:** 23 Rue Lepic, 75018 Paris, France\n\n### Summary\n- For lunch and dinner, **Le Baratin** is highly recommended for its authentic French cuisine and excellent reviews.\n- For accommodation, **Le Marais Boutique** and **Montmartre Suites** fit within your budget.\n\nLet me know if you need any further assistance or if you'd like to make reservations!"
